              "details": "Zod schema-validation library through 4.6.5 contains an uncontrolled resource consumption vulnerability that allows attackers to exhaust memory by submitting a large array to an application using an array schema without a length constraint. Attackers can exploit the handleArrayResult parse logic in $ZodArray, which accumulates every validation issue for each failing element with no cap or early termination, causing the process to allocate excessive issue objects and crash due to out-of-memory conditions.",
              "id": "GHSA-mrhx-c7xc-m3w5",
              "modified": "2026-10-23T18:30:09.376405885Z",
              "published": "2026-10-01T18:32:46Z",
